## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* **a differing, added or removed customer name, link text, href, label, caption, notice, button word, stage word, date or printed figure beyond the proved list of 15 strings (and the three reused labels); the caption bytes changed; a row that prints a current figure without its target; `parseRegister` that THROWS on any input or RETURNS a value that is not exactly the stored shape with every entry trimmed and passing `checkEntry`; a prototype reached by a `__proto__` or `constructor` key; "Verified complete" accepted without an evidence reference on any path (store, screen, parse-back); anything written before the check passes, or written on a refusal; any storage other than the one key, any cookie, any request made by the register, any second tab sharing the value; an existing test modified, a path beyond the 9 vs `332dcc6f`, a byte differing from main in the C1 byte-equal list, an export removed or renamed, a `data-testid`, `id`, heading id, accessible name, handler, `href` or route changed or lost; the override flow, its audit note or `TIERS`/`TIERS_EXPLAINED` changed; `RoadmapBoard` rendering the register; a page wider than the viewport on any cell at comb that is not wider at main; a NEW axe serious/critical; a NEW control under 44 px; the unit suite, lint, typecheck, build or shard check failing at comb and not at main; PART 1 failing lint, typecheck, build or any unit row alone (C4: the split is broken); a role/session/cookie/storage read or write beyond the one key (STOP, tier 1); a reproduced red (3 of 3 alone); the head moved; a NEW CodeQL alert; a check-run of the head `failure`; a secret; a person's name, card id or `B###` token in an added line or a commit message; a request to any origin other than your loopback ports; an implied HP-tool integration or a claim the register is saved on a server or feeds a customer view.** *Major:* **the revert of `9009d8c` conflicting or not giving part 1's tree byte-for-byte (C4b: the split path is broken); p1 to p6 or p14 to p17 surviving (a plant that changes the refusal rule, trimming, write order, the network, the label, the register's placement, the parse rejection, the never-throw guard, the prototype guard or the second storage and stays green in BOTH the unit suite and your programs); a class the PR adds that is NOT emitted in comb's built CSS (C6); a contrast pair under 4.5:1 (3:1 for a border or ring); a path shared with another open PR or live lane that changes how these screens read, not named by you with what you could not test; a merge-tree conflict with main or the combined tree red; a count contradicted with a verdict consequence; a refusal reachable on screen that shows only a bare label as its message (Q-B ruling accepted the words, not a reachable instance); the register unusable when storage is blocked or when a hostile value is stored (a page error, a blank page).** *Minor/Note/Condition:* **the roadmap 2-up at 1280 and 1440 where main was 4-up (Q-D, accepted: a Note naming the numbers); p7 to p13, p18 to p20 surviving (a class, size or limit pin gap); no cap on the number of stored keys; free text typed into the register lives in the tab's storage with no warning against personal data (a hand-off for the product owner); the duplicate `OWNER_MAX`/`EVIDENCE_MAX` constants in the screen and the store; the row `key` remount after hydration; the refusal text shown twice (field error and status region) if a screen reader reads both; the Feedback pill over a card or a select in a full-page capture (shell, identical class at main: reproduce; Note); the 9 Edge-runtime build lines identical at main (Note); the PR body sentences now wrong or missing (Minor, text, replacements in FOR TUESDAY); the READY line's "0 behind", the stale `PROGRESS` first line, the builder's 15-path versus 9-path shared counts (Notes); the merge ref freshness; unsigned commits (Note); `CodeQL` `neutral` that turns `success` (Note, explained); CI/CodeQL PENDING at the verdict, or `CodeQL` still `neutral` (Condition); local fonts vs the runner (Note); the existing a11y journey timeout under load, identical at main (Note, a ticket).** Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the plant, the row, the input and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C8 and C10 measured with their controls, zero findings above Note, every `Analyze (<language>)` complete at `9009d8c0` (or on the merge ref) with open alerts zero (control fired), `CodeQL` concluded and explained, every check-run `success`; GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only (an open item named on the line above the last line; the 15 strings and the hand-offs in FOR TUESDAY are the product owner's to veto or schedule); **NO GO on any Blocker or Major = NO GO round 1 of 2 on this class**, with the fix-shape in prose (round 2 is a fix kit; not the cap) and the LANDING SHAPE (`part 1 only` when part 1 is green alone and every finding sits in `9009d8c`'s four files). A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP, and G2 then escalates to tier 1.
